  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Glibenclamide (glyburide) is a sulfonylurea anti-diabetic medicine used to lower blood sugar in diabetes, including a form of maturity-onset diabetes of the young. It is an approved medicine, appears on the WHO essential medicines list, and is authorised in the European Union for diabetes.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q420626&quot;>Wikidata Q420626</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>glibenclamide</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A10BB01</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01016&quot;>DB01016</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/3488&quot;>3488</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q420626&quot;>Q420626</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C23H28ClN3O5S</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>494.003 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
end Glibenclamide;
